e how are you  different from other data scientists  what are you really good at  max i understand one of your team  members is going to speak at pi data  global  are you excited to see their talk can  you tell us a little bit about what  they'll be speaking about  yes it's actually one of the people that  i work with closely  she's called lorraine del meda  she's a data scientist working in london  actually our team is spread out over  multiple places  and she will be talking about entity  matching  advanced entity matching at scale  i can introduce a topic shortly that we  we of course as a bank we have a lot of  transactions  coming in and going out for example  we're interested  in uh when you have outgoing  transactions we want to know if say the  names on those transactions if they can  actually  be connected to any known clients at ing  to get a better picture of a full  picture of a client  so that's actually a very  computationally difficult problem has a  lot of interesting data science angles  so we want to match names to node names  and it's  it's a big problem very interesting  please take a look  so max is there any final words you'd  like to leave with the pi data global  community  uh yes please go check out there are two  talks  by ing given it by data global please go  check them out they're very interesting  maybe also please check out the open  source contributions by ing  you can find them at githubgithub.com  ing bank  and please contribute to open source  thank you everybody for joining us  in this pi data global sponsor interview  with max bach from ing bank  it was really interesting hearing a  little bit about how ing bank uses these  open source tools  and i'm very happy to hear that ing is a  big supporter not only of our pi data  meetup and conferences but also of the  pi data ecosystem itself in the form of  making direct contributions back to the  projects  and originating their own open source  projects thanks max  thanks james much a